[size=4][i]Let your magic tattoos glisten.[/i][/size]

[size=5][b]Description[/b][/size]

This patch connects [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] (MTF) to [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/78804]Wet Function Redux SE[/url]. A tattoo tier can show only when the skin is soaked, once a sweat has built up, or while someone is drying off after a swim. A tier can also wet or dry the skin when it appears, or make everyone sweat and dry faster while it shows.

It adds a [b]Wet Function Redux[/b] plugin to MTF's menu and to Magic Tattoos UI. Wet Function Redux itself is not changed.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/180775]Magic Tattoos Framework[/url] 0.7.0 or later, and its requirements
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/78804]Wet Function Redux SE[/url]. Built against 1.0 (script version 39). Works with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/108511]OSweat[/url] patch too.
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/13048]PapyrusUtil SE[/url]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Install with your mod manager and enable [font=Courier New]MTF_Plugin_WetFunction.esp[/font]. It is ESL-flagged and only lists [font=Courier New]Skyrim.esm[/font] and [font=Courier New]MagicTattoosFramework.esp[/font] as masters, so it can go anywhere after MTF. Wet Function Redux is found at runtime; if it isn't loaded, the plugin stays unregistered and does nothing.

[size=5][b]Conditions[/b][/size]

Conditions work on any actor Wet Function Redux tracks, the player or NPCs. An actor it has never run on has no wetness, so every condition is false for them.

[list]
[*][b]Wetness[/b]: wetness is at least 0 to 100% of Wet Function's maximum ("cap" in its MCM)
[*][b]Wetness stage[/b]: the skin is Dry, Sweaty, or Soaked, matched exactly, "or wetter", or "or drier"
[*][b]Wetness trend[/b]: the actor is getting wetter, or drying off
[*][b]Wet Function running[/b]: Wet Function's effect is running on the actor
[/list]

The stages use Wet Function's own "start" and "soaked" points. Wet Function holds its sweaty look a little longer while drying, so the visuals can lag slightly behind the stage condition. The trend is only known while Wet Function's effect runs on the actor.

[size=5][b]Effects[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Wet the skin[/b] ([i]once[/i]): raises wetness by 1 to 100% of the maximum
[*][b]Dry the skin[/b] ([i]once[/i]): lowers wetness by 1 to 100% of the maximum
[*][b]Wetness rate[/b] ([i]while shown[/i]): Wet Function's global rate runs at 10 to 500%, for getting wet and drying alike
[/list]

Wetting and drying work on the player and NPCs, but only on actors Wet Function tracks. A forced wetness (the Force slider in Wet Function's MCM) overrides them, as it overrides Wet Function's own sources.

Wetness rate changes Wet Function's "Global rate multiplier", which applies to everyone, so it only does something on a player tier. Several tiers with it multiply together, and each puts its share back when it stops. Avoid moving the Global rate multiplier slider while such a tier is showing.

[size=5][b]Uninstalling[/b][/size]

Take off any tattoo whose tiers use Wetness rate, so the multiplier is put back, then save, quit, and disable the plugin.

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

The Papyrus log ([font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/Logs/Script/Papyrus.0.log[/font]) should show [font=Courier New][MTF_Main] Registered 'proteux-mtf.wetfunction'[/font] a few seconds after loading a save. If it doesn't, check that Wet Function Redux and MTF are enabled and that [font=Courier New]MTF_Plugin_WetFunction.esp[/font] loads after [font=Courier New]MagicTattoosFramework.esp[/font].

[url=https://github.com/proteux/skyrim-magic-tattoo-connectors/blob/main/connectors/wetfunction/TESTING.md]TESTING.md[/url] walks through checking each condition and effect in game.

